despite television being a very crowded  field right now the police procedural  series ncis  is still going strong in its 18th season  and even today  it's one of the most watched shows in  america loyal viewers have stuck with  the series since its premiere in 2003  and in its 10th season it even surpassed  sunday night football and american idol  to become the highest rated broadcast on  network tv  since that time ncis has never left the  list of top 3 most watched shows in the  country it even inspired two spin-offs  of its own  ncis new orleans and ncis los angeles  both of which are hugely popular in  their own right unsurprisingly for a  massively successful show that's been on  the air for nearly two decades ncis has  also seen its fair share of behind the  scenes drama  perhaps most contentious of all however  was showrunner and creator donald  belisario's sudden departure from the  show in 2007.  after less than five years why would  someone leave such a successful show  and one they created too well let's just  say it wasn't exactly by choice  it's worth knowing a little more about  belisario's background in television  after all his name is practically  synonymous with the medium his writing  career began in 1977 when he earned his  first credit for penning an  episode of the cliff potts lead series  big hawaii on nbc  he continued to bolster his resume  throughout the late 70s as a writer and  director contributing to some of the  most well-known tv shows of the decade  including kojak battlestar galactica and  quincy me  belisario's big break arrived in 1980  when he launched his first series magnum  pi which became a cultural staple for  american tv and established tom selleck  as a household name  the show was an enormous success for cbs  and remained on the air for eight  seasons this was just the beginning of  belisario's working relationship with  the network however which would continue  on and off for nearly 40 years  despite the runaway success of magnum pi  bellisario's name wasn't exactly a  golden ticket to success for his tv  creations  tales of the golden monkey an abc  adventure show attempting to capitalize  on the success of raiders of the lost  ark  aired for only one season in 1982-83  another one of his works was tequila and  bonnetti a cbs comedy drama about an  italian cop and his talking canine  partner  amid poor reviews from critics the  network canceled the show before the  last two of its 12 filmed  episodes could air still after that  rough patch he rebounded with more hits  including the cult favorite science  fiction series quantum leap which  debuted in 1989.  the show survived for four seasons with  the final episode attracting almost 13  million viewers  but his biggest success even above  magnum pi would come in 1995 with the  debut of jag  nbc is probably still kicking themselves  to this day over that one only the first  season of jag  aired on their network and when they  opted to drop the show cbs swooped in  what followed was a popular 10 season  run but more importantly thanks to a  backdoor pilot in season 8 and cis was  born spinning off to quickly become the  juggernaut franchise it is today but  belisario's time with ncis came to a  dramatic end  when in 2007 the show star mark harman  forced him out  according to reports the two butted  heads for months with harman disliking  belisario's quote  chaotic management style and the long  hours that resulted from it the network  decided harman's star power was more  important to the show than belisario's  behind the scenes work  and the latter was subsequently fired  however he retained an executive  producer title on the show which he  still holds today  this wasn't the end of the drama  involving belisario though the ex-show  runner sued cbs after ncis los angeles  entered into production  an existing clause in his contract gave  him the right to create the show's first  spin-off but after his forced departure  from the show cbs hired fellow ncis  executive producer shane brennan to make  it instead needless to say bellisario  was not  okay with this everything is not okay  belisario and cbs ultimately settled out  of court for an  undisclosed amount belisario is now  retired from tv and although he may no  longer be actively involved with ncis  fans still have him to thank for  creating and producing such a  long-running and beloved series  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

